  <section class="market-definition-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-label">The direct answer</div>
      <h2>What are US market entry sales services?</h2>
      <p><strong>US market entry sales services help an international company turn an expansion idea into a practical customer acquisition motion.</strong></p>
      <p>CallTeam works on the commercial side of entry: market segments, target accounts, buyer roles, sales language, outbound outreach, qualification, meetings, and the evidence created by real conversations.</p>
      <p>The objective is not a report that sits in a folder. It is a clearer answer to three questions: who responds, why they care, and what it takes to create a serious next step.</p>
      <div class="market-scope-note"><strong>Scope:</strong> CallTeam provides sales development and market validation. Legal, tax, immigration, employment, entity, and regulatory decisions require qualified specialists.</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="market-risk-section">
    <div class="container-wide">
      <div class="section-label">Why expansion plans stall</div>
      <h2>The US is not one giant list of possible customers.</h2>
      <p class="market-section-intro">A large addressable market can hide a weak entry plan. These are the problems that waste time before a sales motion has a chance to learn.</p>
      <div class="market-risk-grid">
        <article><span>01</span><h3>The home market message is copied over</h3><p>Buyers may use different language, expect different proof, and compare the offer against different alternatives.</p></article>
        <article><span>02</span><h3>The entire country becomes the target</h3><p>Industry, company size, buyer role, region, use case, and timing are left too broad to produce a useful signal.</p></article>
        <article><span>03</span><h3>Data is mistaken for demand</h3><p>A database can identify accounts. It cannot confirm attention, relevance, objections, urgency, or willingness to meet.</p></article>
        <article><span>04</span><h3>Credibility is not translated</h3><p>Proof that works at home may need stronger context before an unfamiliar US buyer understands why it matters.</p></article>
        <article><span>05</span><h3>Hiring happens before validation</h3><p>A new salary and tool stack cannot repair an unclear segment, weak message, or offer the market does not yet understand.</p></article>
        <article><span>06</span><h3>Nobody captures the feedback</h3><p>Calls, objections, referrals, timing, and lost interest disappear instead of guiding the next campaign decision.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

