  <section id="faq" class="market-faq-section">
    <div class="container-wide">
      <div class="section-label">US market entry FAQ</div>
      <h2>Questions international B2B companies ask before selling into the US.</h2>
      <div class="market-faq-list">
        <details><summary>What are US market entry sales services?</summary><p>US market entry sales services help a company turn expansion plans into a working sales motion. The work can include market segmentation, target account research, buyer mapping, message adaptation, outbound outreach, qualification, appointment setting, and market feedback.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Can CallTeam help a company outside the United States find US customers?</summary><p>Yes. CallTeam works with B2B companies outside the United States that want to test demand, reach US decision makers, build qualified pipeline, and learn what the market requires before or during expansion.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Do we need a US office before testing sales demand?</summary><p>A company can often begin market research and sales outreach before building a full US office. The correct legal, tax, employment, entity, and compliance setup depends on the company and should be reviewed with qualified specialists. CallTeam provides sales execution, not legal or tax advice.</p></details>
        <details><summary>How does CallTeam help find the first US customers?</summary><p>CallTeam turns the ideal customer hypothesis into specific US segments, accounts, and buyer roles. We then use calling led outreach and approved follow up to start conversations, qualify interest, schedule useful meetings, and capture market evidence.</p></details>
        <details><summary>How do we choose the first US market segment?</summary><p>Start with the strongest overlap between a painful business problem, credible proof, reachable accounts, relevant buyer roles, commercial value, and the company's ability to deliver. The first campaign should be narrow enough to learn from.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Does CallTeam build the US prospect list?</summary><p>CallTeam can build or refine the target account and contact universe, or work from a client CRM, account list, event list, inbound source, partner list, or previous campaign.</p></details>
        <details><summary>How will CallTeam represent our company?</summary><p>CallTeam works from an approved campaign brief, positioning, proof, talk track, qualification standard, follow up, claims, and clear boundaries. The client approves the commercial foundation before outreach begins.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Which outreach channels are used?</summary><p>CallTeam is calling led because live conversations expose market fit, language, objections, roles, timing, and next steps. Approved email follow up and other agreed channels can support the campaign depending on the engagement.</p></details>
        <details><summary>How are US meetings qualified?</summary><p>The criteria are agreed before launch and can include account fit, role relevance, business reason, current approach, interest, timing, decision path, authority, and a clear purpose for the next conversation.</p></details>
        <details><summary>What market feedback will we receive?</summary><p>The campaign can capture segment response, buyer language, common objections, credibility gaps, role corrections, timing, referrals, meeting quality, follow up needs, and reasons opportunities do or do not move.</p></details>
        <details><summary>How long does a US market entry campaign take?</summary><p>The right duration depends on the market size, number of hypotheses, data quality, buyer seniority, contact rates, sales cycle, offer complexity, and the amount of evidence required. CallTeam defines the work after reviewing the market entry question.</p></details>
        <details><summary>How much do US market entry sales services cost?</summary><p>Pricing depends on the market scope, number of segments, research and list requirements, buyer seniority, outreach workload, qualification depth, CRM workflow, reporting, and the amount of market testing required.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Which countries can CallTeam support?</summary><p>CallTeam can support B2B companies from many regions that want to sell into the United States, provided the offer, target buyer, language, market access, and commercial setup are suitable for the campaign.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Is this only for the US or for North America?</summary><p>This service is built around entering the United States. A broader North American campaign can be discussed when the target market and sales logic support it, but the scope should stay specific enough to produce useful evidence.</p></details>
        <details><summary>When is CallTeam not the right fit?</summary><p>The service may not be right when the offer has no credible value, the target buyer cannot be defined, the company cannot support US sales conversations or delivery, legal and commercial readiness are unresolved, or the objective is activity without market learning.</p></details>
        <details><summary>How do we start?</summary><p>Start with a strategy call. We review the offer, existing proof, current markets, US hypotheses, buyer roles, data, sales capacity, qualification standard, systems, and the decision the campaign needs to support.</p></details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cta-band market-final-cta">
    <div class="section-label">Turn the US plan into market evidence</div>
